// FROST FORTRESS — ABSOLUTE ZERO — one song: what it plays, how it is arranged, how it sounds.
//
// THE BANGER. FROST FORTRESS as festival big-room house — a game alternate of frost,
// selectable from the dev menu (GAME ALTERNATES) and on the desk. Nothing replaces the
// live song.
// 
// Frost's hook is one bar — D F A F D, then C E leading back to D — and here it is the
// hook of a main-stage drop: an electric grand with a plain square doubling it, an ice
// bell an octave over, supersaws pumping on every beat, four on the floor, an offbeat
// bass. The drop grows the one bar into eight by sequencing it up the scale (a third,
// then a fifth) and ending on a Gm–A turnaround, so the hook itself is every other bar.
// The intro and outro are the original nearly verbatim — its Dm–G dorian vamp, its pad
// voicing, its offbeat bass walk D A B F | G D G A. Drop two is a DOUBLE drop: eight
// harder bars in D minor, a stop, then frost's own trick — up a major third into F#
// minor, as the original does in bars 17–20.
// 
//   1–4    intro — the original vamp, grand hook, polar-drift pad (the cabinet-screen loop)
//   5–8    build — Dm | Bb C; snare roll quarters to sixteenths, filter opening, riser
//   9–24   drop — the hook grown to eight bars, twice; the bell octave in the second half
//   25–28  breakdown — the hook at half speed over a D pedal: Dm9 Bbmaj9 Gm9 Cadd9
//   29–32  build two
//   33–40  drop two — harder: mega-saw doubling, crystal sixteenths, a stop at the end
//   41–56  drop three — the lift into F# minor: grand in octaves, choir, everything
//   57–60  outro — the original vamp; the loop returns to bar 5 (the build)
// 
// Cabinet sync kept: frost-3's sleigh carol takes its key from the first bass note of
// the section it lands in, so every bar pair starts on the tonic (D, or F# in the lift);
// the generator asserts it. 128 keeps the carol's eight beats inside the flypast.
// 
// 60 bars at 128, 113s. Written by
// work/local/_frost-remix-absolute-zero.mjs through work/local/_remix-lib.mjs;
// re-running it rewrites this file.
//
// SPOT FX (1 Oct 2026, work/local/_spot-fx-stops.mjs): the stop at the end of bar 40 cuts the drums, bass and chords under the held hook and the riser, into the F# minor lift.
//
// SPOT FX — MORE (1 Oct 2026, work/local/_spot-fx-more.mjs): the build (5–8) opens a lowpass on the whole mix an eighth at a time; stutter rolls on beat 3 of 8 and 32.
//
// The music below is the composition. Everything under THE DESK WRITES BELOW HERE
// is written by `npm run mixer` and will be rewritten on every save — put notes
// about the song up here, where they survive.
